Marina, Distance uses a bias correction when taking the exponential=20
which probably explains why you don't get the same result for E^(s) when=20
you regress log(s) on x.  I'm not sure why you're rescaling g.  It=20
should simply be the detection function evaluated at x for a cluster at=20
distance x from the line.  Having estmated the detection function, it=20
does not require rescaling.  It sounds like your estimates of detection=20
probability must differ from those Distance obtains.

Steve

